  "authoringNote": "No encounter version is supplied at all, and no placeholder sidecar stands in for it. With no current usable encounter and no restricted, unreadable or failed-provenance encounter candidate, R04 holds R04.no_usable_encounter, missing for the authorization coordinator, naming no document; a missing finding names no parent (C07). R09 passes with no condition: nothing restricted or unreadable is fabricated for an absent record, which keeps this absence finding distinct from access denial (F16a) and unreadability (F16c). R04 reads only final current usable documents (recorded reading of C05 and C09), so it cites the final order's status, date and practitioner identifier (three) and nothing from the encounter. No encounter is supplied, so R02 binds only the order and receipt and cites their beneficiary facts (four). R01 (eight citations), R03 (nine) and R05 (four; the receipt follows the order date span 2026-09-01T10:00Z to 2026-09-03T12:00Z under C06) pass. R06 stays qualified clinical review with no clinical citation and no administrative effect: an unavailable record is not evidence that any clinical fact is absent, and no negative clinical assertion is made. R07 passes with no citation because neither the case nor a current usable encounter states LCMP incorporation; that pass asserts nothing about the content of the unavailable record. R08 passes and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_information, blocked by R04 alone.",
